     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">From: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">Danilo Brandão</span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><br></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">Dear All,</span><br style=\"line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">I would like some suggestions on a regime switching model i&#39;m trying to implement. It&#39;s a time series model where only my transition equation is regime dependent. Although, when i try to define the noise object i get the following message</span><br style=\"line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><br style=\"line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">&quot;Oi, Chap! I found 1 regime for &#39;values.observed&#39; but 2 regimes elsewhere, so I extended the observed covariances to match.</span><br style=\"line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">If this is what you wanted, all is sunshine and puppy dogs.&quot;</span><br style=\"line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><br style=\"line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">Another issue that i encoutered is how to implement formulas in the factor loading matrix as in the spirit of Nelson-Siegel models form term structure(Levant &amp; Ma(2016); Caldeira(2016) and others)</span><br style=\"line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><br style=\"line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">Thanks for your attention</span><br></div><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Michael D. Hunter, PhD</span><br style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Assistant Professor of Quantitative Psychology</span></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Georgia Institute of Technology<br style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><div dir=\"ltr\">J.S. Coon Building, Room 225</div></span></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">E-mail: </span><a href style=\"font-size:12.8px\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mhunt...@gmail.com</a> or <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mhun...@gatech.edu</a><br></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
